{"conjecture": "Software systems calcify because APIs are frozen at the moment of first integration rather than at the moment of demonstrated stability, forcing every subsequent feature change to propagate through boundaries that were never validated against future use cases. This couples conceptually unrelated changes: modifying capability X requires updating integration points for capabilities Y and Z simply because they share a frozen boundary, even though their domain logic is independent. The review and testing process enforces this coupling by verifying that each change conforms to the existing boundary contract, thereby validating calcification rather than preventing it."}
